<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shaoxing</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shaoxing is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a> Bay. As Kuaiji it was the centre of the ancient State of Yue, and nearby Mount Kuaiji is the traditional burial place of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yu-the-great">Yu the Great</a>. The city is known for its canals, its Shaoxing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> wine and as the birthplace of the writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lu-xun">Lu Xun</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shaoxing.jpg" alt="Shaoxing" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zhangzhugang · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shaoxing_Bazi_Qiao_2017.12.09_16-16-06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
